;; `test/cljs` is a source path rather than a per-build one because shadow-cljs
;; has only the top-level list — and it costs the app build nothing: a browser
;; build compiles what its `:init-fn` reaches, and nothing in the app requires a
;; test.
;;
;; The two `../us-vs-them` paths are here for the same reason and by the same
;; road **music takes to corvo** (`music/shadow-cljs.edn`: `"../corvo/src/lib"`
;; on this same list): a sibling checkout whose ClojureScript this build
;; compiles from source. `deps.edn` already names the library
;; `{:local/root "../us-vs-them"}` for the *server*, and this file does not read
;; `deps.edn` — shadow-cljs has its own `:source-paths` and `:dependencies` —
;; so without these two lines the library was simply invisible to
;; ClojureScript, which is what it was until the caution port.
;;
;; Switching this build to `:deps true` instead would have made one road out of
;; two, and was not worth it: it drags the whole server tree — jetty, sqlite,
;; ragtime, buddy — onto the ClojureScript compile classpath to reach two
;; namespaces, and it changes how every other build in this file resolves in
;; order to fix one that does not.
;;
;; **The two paths fail differently when they are not there, and that decided
;; the Docker story.** `../us-vs-them/src` is load-bearing: `et.cb.caution` is
;; on the app's own require graph now, so a missing `src` is a compile error and
;; the deploy stops. `plurama/Dockerfile` already copies it to
;; `/opt/us-vs-them` before `cd cookbook && npx shadow-cljs release app`,
;; because the uberjar needed it first — so the production build needs no change
;; at all for this. `../us-vs-them/test` is *not* load-bearing and shadow-cljs
;; ignores a source path that does not exist without a word, which was checked
;; rather than assumed: a release build with that directory moved away completes
;; clean. So the image does not carry the library's tests and does not need to.
;;
;; The cost of that silence is that `make test-cljs` would quietly shrink if the
;; sibling's `test` went away, so cookbook does not rely on it for the thing
;; cookbook cares about: **`et.cb.ui.provenance-test`** pins the adapter on this
;; host by itself, and it is in `test/cljs`, which is not a sibling of anything.
;; (Not `et.cb.caution-test` — that is the JVM suite in `test/unit`, on no
;; ClojureScript source path at all, and it is a different guard for a different
;; host. The two are deliberately named alike and are not interchangeable.)
{:source-paths ["src/cljs" "src/cljc" "test/cljs"
                "../us-vs-them/src" "../us-vs-them/test"]
 :dependencies [[reagent "2.0.1"]
                [cljs-ajax "0.8.4"]]
 :http {:port #shadow/env ["SHADOW_PORT" :as :int :default 9807]}
 :builds {:app {:target :browser
                :output-dir "resources/public/cookbook/js"
                :asset-path "/js"
                :modules {:main {:init-fn et.cb.ui.core/init}}
                :devtools {:repl-pprint true}}
          ;; `make test-cljs`, and two drift controls in it rather than one.
          ;;
          ;; The first is the seal envelope, implemented twice — here on
          ;; WebCrypto, and in plurama-cli on javax.crypto — where the only
          ;; honest guard against two spellings of one control drifting apart is
          ;; a fixture both suites read. Node has WebCrypto natively, so the
          ;; envelope needs no browser to be pinned; the key store does, and is
          ;; checked in the browser instead.
          ;;
          ;; The second is `caution`. Cookbook now computes the provenance split
          ;; in two hosts — the server for a published Recipe, the browser for a
          ;; sealed one — off one `.cljc` source, and this is where the browser's
          ;; half is exercised: `et.cb.ui.provenance-test` for cookbook's adapter
          ;; and `local-split`, and `et.uvt.caution-test` for the arithmetic under
          ;; it, which arrives over the sibling source path above and is the
          ;; library's own specification rather than a second copy of it.
          ;; cookbook's *other* caution suite, `et.cb.caution-test`, is JVM-only
          ;; and runs under `make test`; nothing here can reach it.
          :test {:target :node-test
                 :output-to "target/node-tests.js"
                 :ns-regexp "-test$"}}}
